        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alsea%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Hayden Bridge, listed on the National Register of Historic Places, carries Hayden Road over the river near Alsea.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alsea%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "While logging was once the primary industry in Alsea, the area is now known for steelhead fishing on the Alsea River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alsea%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Alsea sits on the banks of the Alsea River on Highway 34, roughly twenty-six miles from Corvallis.",
